% -e over a rule that derives nothing, its head restated in its body behind
% a demand call: p(a)? adorns p with its column bound, and the call p(X),
% made after q(X), reads p's b adornment with the head's own argument.  The
% call has no magic rule and no cut before it, so the adorned rule reads its
% head and is dropped, and p is derived by its fact alone.

r(a).
r(b).

q(X) :- r(X).

p(a).
p(X) :- q(X), p(X).

p(a)?
